From f6fe2e8fe6fd5d1ab5d12c8ef8a894c7a64cfe35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:52:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 683/687] test(engram): read the truncated row file past the
 reader's row cache

Base: candidate-38's patch head 753354cf4 (tree 37b34b8f), the series of
experiments/2026-10-26-spark-ds41f-candidate/candidate-38/vllm/series.

Rationale: test_disk_engram_preparation_refreshes_graph_and_rejects_stale_rows
truncates one table's row file and expects the next step's read to fail with
"short Engram row read". Since the reader gained a user-space row cache
(56873181ff, #759 and #754: a 4-way set-associative cache of the rows it has
read, filled after every step), a step whose rows were all read before is
served from the cache and reads no file. The test's last steps reuse the ids of
the step before them, so the truncation went unread: failure() stayed None for
the test's 30 s wait and its `in` check raised TypeError. The same failure was
reported on candidate-36's image (#846).

The test now builds its disk reader with cache_rows=0: the Engram module's
EngramDiskRows name is patched with that partial before the model is made (the
reader opens in process_weights_after_loading), so every step of the test reads
the files and the truncation is read. The cache is right to serve what it has
(a checkpoint is immutable while serving); its own tests are
tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_engram_rows.py.

Quality: no runtime change; a test-only patch.

Tests: tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py in spark-ds41f:candidate-38 on
dgx4 (GB10): 43 passed (was 42 passed, 1 failed).

Upstream status: not applicable; the disk Engram reader and its tests are this
deployment's.
---
 tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py b/tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py
index 33be3b2284..753ea9690c 100644
--- a/tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py
+++ b/tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
 
+import functools
 import gc
 import json
 import pickle
@@ -427,6 +428,14 @@ def test_disk_engram_preparation_refreshes_graph_and_rejects_stale_rows(
 ):
     """Accepted GPU history, images, padding and failures cross the eager boundary."""
     make_model, weights, paths = tiny_engram_checkpoint
+    # The reader serves rows it has read before from its row cache (a checkpoint
+    # is immutable while serving). Every step of this test reads the files, so
+    # the truncation below is read.
+    monkeypatch.setattr(
+        engram_module,
+        "EngramDiskRows",
+        functools.partial(engram_module.EngramDiskRows, cache_rows=0),
+    )
     root, target, session = make_model("disk")
     resident_root, resident, resident_session = make_model("device")
     _load_checkpoint(root, tmp_path)
